			"date": "2023-04-13T17:27:49.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@colepeters\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>colepeters</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@brianleroux\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>brianleroux</span></a></span> Nice site :)</p><p>I tend to select text a lot for text to speech reasons while browsing and there are a couple weird interactions on the site where illustrative elements are stacking on top of text content</p><p>For example, if the window is &gt; 1000px wide you can't select the text in the paragraph that begins \"Enhance makes the right way the easy way.\" Adding `pointer-events: none;` to the `figure.rainbow-top` element fixes this</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
